From b1ee387e37b66d7ad2676d985b794e4aa2fc9cf8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: chaoso85 <216391968+chaoso85@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 00:13:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] iommu: qcom_iommu: init the TZ secure page-table pool for
 every TZ-managed instance

Part of the reference project used: downstream 3.10 drivers/iommu/msm_iommu_sec.c (LineageOS
android_kernel_sony_msm8994: msm_iommu_sec_ptbl_init() once at init) and qcom_iommu_sec_ptbl_init().
Before: the pool was only set up by an instance with a secure context bank (Venus SMMU). With the Venus SMMU
disabled (patch 0025) the MDP SMMU (qcom,iommu-secure-id = <1>) came up without it; the panel stayed black with
'pp done time out' on every frame. The only boot with a working panel (#14) had the Venus SMMU probe first.

Signed-off-by: chaoso85 <216391968+chaoso85@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c
index a94dfb454c4..5243dab38b9 100644
--- a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c
@@ -1208,7 +1208,15 @@ static int qcom_iommu_device_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		qcom_iommu->non_secure = true;
 	}
 
-	if (qcom_iommu_has_secure_context(qcom_iommu)) {
+	/*
+	 * Downstream 3.10 (msm_iommu_sec.c) sets up the TZ secure page-table
+	 * pool once at init, before any TZ-managed SMMU is programmed. Here it
+	 * used to run only from an instance with a secure context bank (the
+	 * Venus SMMU). With Venus disabled the MDP SMMU (secure-id 1) was
+	 * restored by TZ without it: no faults, but every frame ended in
+	 * "pp done time out" and the panel stayed black. The helper runs once.
+	 */
+	if (qcom_iommu_has_secure_context(qcom_iommu) || !qcom_iommu->non_secure) {
 		ret = qcom_iommu_sec_ptbl_init(dev);
 		if (ret) {
 			dev_err(dev, "cannot init secure pg table(%d)\n", ret);
-- 
